{
 "uid": "qa-bugs",
 "title": "QA Bug Report",
 "tags": [
  "qa"
 ],
 "timezone": "browser",
 "schemaVersion": 39,
 "version": 1,
 "refresh": "",
 "description": "One row per bug with where to fix it, the code line, steps to reproduce and a screenshot.",
 "time": {
  "from": "now-30d",
  "to": "now"
 },
 "links": [
  {
   "title": "Run page",
   "type": "link",
   "url": "${api_url}/runs/${run}",
   "targetBlank": true,
   "icon": "external link"
  },
  {
   "title": "All findings",
   "type": "link",
   "url": "/d/qa-findings/qa-findings?var-run=${run}",
   "icon": "dashboard"
  },
  {
   "title": "Components",
   "type": "link",
   "url": "/d/qa-components/qa-components?var-run=${run}",
   "icon": "dashboard"
  },
  {
   "title": "Runs",
   "type": "link",
   "url": "/d/qa-runs/qa-runs",
   "icon": "dashboard"
  }
 ],
 "templating": {
  "list": [
   {
    "name": "run",
    "label": "Run",
    "type": "query",
    "datasource": {
     "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
     "uid": "qa-postgres"
    },
    "refresh": 2,
    "multi": false,
    "includeAll": false,
    "sort": 0,
    "query": "SELECT id AS __value, id || ' · ' || project || ' · ' || platform || ' · ' || to_char(created_at, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') AS __text FROM runs WHERE status = 'completed' ORDER BY created_at DESC",
    "definition": "SELECT id AS __value, id || ' · ' || project || ' · ' || platform || ' · ' || to_char(created_at, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') AS __text FROM runs WHERE status = 'completed' ORDER BY created_at DESC"
   },
   {
    "name": "api_url",
    "label": "API URL (screenshots, run page)",
    "type": "textbox",
    "query": "http://localhost:8000",
    "current": {
     "text": "http://localhost:8000",
     "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    "options": [
     {
      "text": "http://localhost:8000",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "selected": true
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
 "panels": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 15,
    "h": 9
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### How to read this report\n\n1. **Pick the run** in the *Run* menu above (newest first). The run page with the live log is [here](${api_url}/runs/${run}).\n2. **Bugs to fix** lists one bug per row, most severe first. Each row has everything needed to fix it:\n   * **Fix in**: who changes what. *app code* = the repository's source, *app build* = build configuration (Gradle, AndroidManifest, signing), *backend* = the server the app calls.\n   * **Code**: the file and line, at the exact commit that was tested. Click it to open it in the repository.\n   * **Screenshot** and **Steps to reproduce**: the proof. Click a screenshot to open it full size; scroll the table right for Expected / Actual.\n   * **Expected / Actual / How to fix**: what should happen, what happened, and the change that fixes it.\n3. **Held for review** are likely bugs the platform could not confirm on its own (heuristics, emulator-only measurements). Check them, then mark each *real* or *not a bug* on the run page; those labels feed the precision gauge.\n4. **All tests** shows every check that ran, passes included, so you can see what was covered and what was blocked.\n\nSeverity: **critical** crash, data loss or security hole · **high** broken feature or security weakness · **medium** wrong behaviour with a workaround · **low** polish, accessibility, performance."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "This run",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
    "uid": "qa-postgres"
   },
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 15,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 9,
    "h": 9
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
      "uid": "qa-postgres"
     },
     "format": "table",
     "rawQuery": true,
     "editorMode": "code",
     "rawSql": "SELECT\n  r.platform AS \"Platform\",\n  CASE WHEN r.platform = 'web' THEN r.live_url ELSE trim(coalesce(r.stats::jsonb->'build'->>'app_id', '') || ' ' || coalesce(r.stats::jsonb->'build'->>'version', '')) END AS \"Tested build / URL\",\n  coalesce(left(r.commit_sha, 10), '-') AS \"Code commit\",\n  coalesce(r.framework, '-') AS \"Framework\",\n  to_char(r.finished_at, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') AS \"Finished\"\nFROM runs r WHERE r.id = '${run}'",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ],
   "options": {
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "/.*/",
     "values": false
    },
    "textMode": "value_and_name",
    "colorMode": "none",
    "graphMode": "none",
    "justifyMode": "auto",
    "orientation": "horizontal",
    "wideLayout": true
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "color": {
      "mode": "fixed",
      "fixedColor": "text"
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   }
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Bugs",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
    "uid": "qa-postgres"
   },
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 9,
    "w": 12,
    "h": 4
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
      "uid": "qa-postgres"
     },
     "format": "table",
     "rawQuery": true,
     "editorMode": "code",
     "rawSql": "SELECT\n  count(*) FILTER (WHERE status IN ('reported', 'confirmed')) AS \"Bugs to fix\",\n  count(*) FILTER (WHERE status IN ('reported', 'confirmed') AND severity IN ('critical', 'high')) AS \"Critical + high\",\n  count(*) FILTER (WHERE status = 'needs_review') AS \"Held for review\"\nFROM findings WHERE run_id = '${run}'",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ],
   "options": {
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    },
    "textMode": "value_and_name",
    "colorMode": "background",
    "graphMode": "none",
    "orientation": "vertical"
   },
